        0:commonHint('Misreading decimal place value','The number of decimal places is not reflected in the denominator.','Two digits after the decimal point means hundredths: 75/100.','Use a 10 by 10 hundred grid and shade 75 squares.','Ask whether 0.75 means tenths or hundredths.'),
        2:commonHint('Dropping a digit while converting','The decimal may have been treated as 7.5 instead of 0.75.','0.75 is less than one, so its fraction must be less than one.','Place 0.75 on a number line between 0 and 1.','Ask the learner to estimate before converting.'),
        3:commonHint('Confusing 0.75 with 0.25','A familiar quarter fraction may have been recalled without checking the decimal.','0.75 is three quarters; 0.25 is one quarter.','Shade 75 of 100 squares and compare with 25 squares.','Ask the learner to state the decimal for one quarter.')
