        0:commonHint('Adding instead of subtracting','The learner may have combined the amounts rather than finding what remains.','“Remains” means subtract the amount consumed from the starting amount.','Draw a bar for 3/4 and remove 1/3 using twelfths.','Ask which operation matches the word “remains”.'),
        2:commonHint('Subtracting without a common denominator','The learner may be subtracting the visible numerators and denominators directly.','Rename both amounts in twelfths: 3/4 = 9/12 and 1/3 = 4/12. Then 9/12 − 4/12 = 5/12.','Partition a bar into twelve equal parts; shade nine and remove four.','Ask the learner to explain why both fractions must use twelfths before subtraction.'),
